    "description": "The CheckoutRequestHandler currently contains one long method that deserializes a checkout request, authenticates the buyer, validates cart contents, loads inventory and shipping information, calculates the total, reserves stock, records the order, and renders a response. Operations are currently interleaved, so a timeout during stock reservation cannot be attributed to a distinct stage, and replacing authentication requires editing the method. The revised design must name each stage, pass the output of one stage to the next, and permit a stage to be logged, timed, retried, or substituted without changing its neighbors. Authentication and persistence necessarily use external systems, while validation and total calculation can remain deterministic. The stage sequence must support an early rejection after validation without running persistence, and it must not force all intermediate request data into a single mutable object.",
    "decision_statement": "Should the handler be decomposed into independently replaceable named stages with an explicit order, or retained as one method with local intermediate variables?",
    "notes": "pipeline fits the named attributable checkout stages with per-stage observability and early rejection; function-composition is the near miss for the linear chain shape, with functional-core-imperative-shell supporting the deterministic/external split."
  },
